<div class="ltx_pagination ltx_role_newpage"></div>
<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>Experiments and Hyperparameters</h2>

<section id="A1.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.1 </span>GLUE Benchmark</h3>

<div id="A1.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To keep results consistent, we use the same <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\dagger" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>†</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\dagger</annotation></semantics></math> setup as <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib20" title="" class="ltx_ref">Hu et al. [2022]</a></cite> for RoBERTa Large. All of our GLUE experiments have the same max sequence length and epochs for each task.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A1.T4" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering" style="font-size:80%;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table"><span id="A1.T4.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:113%;">Table 4</span>: </span><span id="A1.T4.6" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:113%;">The hyperparameters used for RoBERTa-Large on the GLUE benchmark.</span></figcaption>
<table id="A1.T4.7" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_align_middle">
<tr id="A1.T4.7.1" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A1.T4.7.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_ttt" style="padding-left:5.0pt;padding-right:5.0pt;"><span id="A1.T4.7.1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">Method</span></td>
<td id="A1.T4.7.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_r ltx_border_ttt" style="padding-left:5.0pt;padding-right:5.0pt;"><span id="A1.T4.7.1.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">Dataset</span></td>
